From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:26:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mac host: quit a game by holding the controller's Home button
 (macOS 27)

Quitting a game on the Mac needed Cmd+Q, so a keyboard had to be close.
Holding Home (the logo button on Xbox and PlayStation pads) for 2 seconds
now opens a quit prompt over the game. A quits through the same path as
Cmd+Q (NSApp terminate), B or a new press of Home closes it. Letting go
before 2 seconds does nothing, and a small indicator at the top fills up
while Home is held. While the prompt is open the game gets no controller
input and is told it lost the focus, as the Switch's HOME menu does.

The host already claims Home with preferredSystemGestureState. macOS 27
respects that when the Home button setting for apps lets the app decide,
macOS 26 makes no promise, so the hold works on macOS 27 only and Cmd+Q
stays the way on macOS 26. DM_HOME_QUIT=0 turns it off. On macOS 27 the
log names the setting once (GCControllerHomeButtonSettingsManager), so a
launcher can tell the player when the system keeps Home for itself.
DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT carries the texts in the player's language.

The state machine (home_quit.h) and the views (home_quit_mac.h) are
tested without a controller or a window (t_home_quit, t_home_quit_mac).

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1084
Reason: Quit a game with the controller's Home button on macOS 27, the launcher's console mode needs it (#336)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#336
